														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4831251">
									

<p>Not a bad series 1 article, notwithstanding the pointless end note. Ultimately, though, this left me feeling cold. The shallowness of the symbolism and on the nose nature of the imagery made it very much come across as someone who had done a little reading on East Asian scroll painting, rather than an actual object that could exist. In the end, this reminded me of nothing so much as <a href="https://www.snopes.com/fact-check/quran-911/">this rather stupid urban legend</a>.</p>
<p>Just as an aside, this article could be improved somewhat by having it anticipate future conflicts, rather than simply describe existing ones. An ending of &quot;the painting changed and now we are trying to decipher what it means&quot; would be far more interesting than &quot;lol too bad it can't be a decoration :)&quot;</p>
<p>-1</p>

