<blockquote>
<p>Posing as an environmental group, they interview and interrogate locals on the appearance and disappearance of these fountains.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>What do these interviews/interrogations actually like&#8230;add narratively here? My concern is that they're going to be either relatively info-dumpy or relatively contentless depending on how co-operative the people being interviewed are.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Don't want to give TOO much away.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>you gotta give <em>everything</em> away here btw like if a reviewer doesn't have a full idea of what your idea actually is, it's very hard for them to judge whether it's a good idea.</p>
<hr />
<p>My concern here is that I have a good idea of what the setting of this story is and I kinda like it; but I don't really have a good idea of where it goes or what you're doing in that space and so I'm not sure whether there's enough narrative meat or sense of this like&#8230;going somewhere and working as a story, y'know?</p>
