														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4831112">
									

<p>Minor concern: why is this an MTF? Like, as far as I can tell, this seems like they're effectively behaving as general custodial staff here that are assigned to a site; whereas an MTF is generally y'know, mobile and expected to respond to situations in all sorts of places and handle all sorts of things? This just feels almost more like 'janitorial duty but on a really bad day'.</p>
<p>I'm also unsure about ending on the mystery here: it's an appealing cliffhanger sure but it feels like it could make this feel unsatisfying to read as it kinda feels like a story bookended by more interesting events (since the start is like&#8230;hammer down dealing with a containment breach and implied cool action scenes; and the ending is an implied investigation into a mysterious arm).</p>
<p>Really my big question here is: what's the interplay between the characters like? It feels like the whole story is riding off the characterisation here and while I have a good idea for what Gilligan is like, I don't really have a feel for what Henry is like or what the dynamic between them is.</p>

							</div>

								
					
