<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">[+]&nbsp;open&nbsp;for&nbsp;crit</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<blockquote>
<p>central narrative: none at the moment but I'm open to ideas</p>
</blockquote>
<p>This is a pretty big dealbreaker for me. A good SCP article to me is a short story about a weird thing and how the Foundation interacts with it</p>
<blockquote>
<p>However, when a person with anomalous abilities touches it, their body will instead turn into a new crystal with glowing runes seemingly etched into it.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>'anomalous' doesn't function as a like&#8230;proper physical category of thing. Treating all kinds of anomalies as being the same kinda&#8230;feels really iffy because like why would memetic/cognitohazards work the same as like, reality bending or like, conceptual anomalies or like a factory that makes teddy bears filled guts or w/e.</p>
<hr />
<p>At the end of the day my big concern is 'crystal that grows more crystal in people' is somewhat cliche and also that you don't really <em>do</em> anything with it. It might be really worth thinking about questions like &quot;what makes this interesting to read about?&quot; and &quot;what challenges does its existence pose for the foundation?&quot; and like, really figure out what you can do here to explore this thing in a more interesting way.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>

