			<div class="content" id="post-content-4831096">
									

<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">[+]&nbsp;Open&nbsp;for&nbsp;crit</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<blockquote>
<p>foundation discovers common abstract mechanism enabling magic. Through prodding it manage to open a door to ES.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Is this a 'mechanism' as in like, a physical machine? or a mechanism as in an abstract process?</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Security is tight and progress becomes harder as they get further in.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>What's the security like here? How does it make progress harder?</p>
<p>This feels&#8230;like a really weird way to solve this problem</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Where did the machines come from and what would happen if they were switched off?</p>
</blockquote>
<p>these are interesting questions for it to raise but it feels like there's nothing here really hinting at any kind of interesting answers to them?</p>
<hr />
<p>My concern here overall is that the narrative here feels very passive: there's not a lot driving the Foundations investigation of this forward so it feels like it might be hard to keep a reader on board during the ride. It might be worth considering what the stakes/conflict are here: like, what happens if the foundation fails? What happens if the foundation succeeds? What forces are trying to prevent the foundation succeeding? Why do the foundation keep working against those forces?</p>
<p>It might be worth considering who is the 'face' of this investigation too: like, who are the characters that are in charge of driving the investigation forward and what are their motivations here?</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>

