			<div class="content" id="post-content-4831082">
									

<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">[+]&nbsp;Open&nbsp;for&nbsp;crit</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<blockquote>
<p>Central narrative:</p>
</blockquote>
<p>What I'm really looking for out of a central narrative section is 'what does the article contain': you've mostly used it to expand on what the SCP does; and I'm left wondering what the Foundation's role in all this is and like&#8230;what the actual article would look like.</p>
<p>Like bear in mind: you're trying to write a short story about a weird thing disguised as a technical report; not an encyclopedia entry on it; and so what you do with the SCP is a lot more important than just what the SCP can do.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>each mind-swap creates a copy of the host of the radio show.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>&quot;mind-swap&quot; implies &quot;the listener and the host swap minds&quot;; but it seems like you mean &quot;the host overwrites the listener's mind&quot; here?</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Once they spread the virus, they turn into ruthless monsters.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Why do they turn into ruthless monsters? What does this look like? Like is it a psychological change? A physical change? Both?</p>
<p>Really my concern here is that it feels like it'd be a lot more interesting to look at what happens when there's this growing hive mind of radio hosts than tacking on a thing about them becoming monsters at the end; but perhaps there's a fun angle where some part of the hive mind growth causes it to happen and the story is almost&#8230;tragedy-like in style, y'know? It's like, us slowly watching a character we like turn from being cool and nice to a radio host to a rabid monster, y'know? As a like commentary on how e.g. stuff like fox news affects people say.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>

